# Environment variable template for running these standards' scripts by hand.
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in real values:
#
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# `.env.local` (and every `.env*` except this example) is gitignored, so a
# real token never reaches version control. Supply only placeholders here,
# and see the Security & Secrets guide for the full policy:
# docs/operations/Security-&-Secrets.md
#
# A token comes from `gh auth token`, never from this file in a commit.

# The repository a script acts on, as owner/name. Unset, it is the one gh
# points at.
# TARGET_REPO=owner/name

# Every script that writes defaults to a dry run. Set false to apply.
# DRY_RUN=true
